<title>MEXICO: Bancomext lowers interest rates on export credits.</title>
<headline>Bancomext lowers interest rates on export credits.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican development bank, Bancomext, said it will lower  the interest rate it charges on credits denominated in U.S. dollars, aiming to give a boost to exports.</p>
<p>The export development bank said the changes would go into effect on July 17 and were brought about by better external financing costs.</p>
<p>The bank said that companies could, for example, receive credits at Libor plus 325 basis points for credits of 10 years, down from the Libor plus 500 basis points it charged before.</p>
<p>((--Robert Kozak, Mexico City newsroom 525 728-9559))</p>
